{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Purchasing or Licensing IT Systems: Tips "}, {"type": "position", "content": 7}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 1}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.3"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use when talking about contracting tips."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Understand information about people's backgrounds in spoken or written documents.    Participate in the improvement of IT contracts, establishing technical clauses that respond to the needs of the negotiating agents, based on current laws on contracting."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of a range of grammar and vocabulary, and with the appropriate level of formality and purpose, coherence and cohesion for the context.   Recognizes simple ideas on concepts on IT contracts and knowledge transfer, simulated processes of IT contracting, and technological negotiation."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe8n7le01ob07re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Verb + ing and to + verb, to talk about Purchasing or Licensing IT Systems"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "Some verbs are followed specifically by -ing or infinitive forms of the verbs."}, {"type": "example", "content": "What determines whether an organization needs to buy or license an IT solution?"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Below, you can find some common verbs that are followed by \u2013ing forms:"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":1,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<p style=\\\"text-align: center;\\\">Avoid<br />Put off<br />Risk<br />Involve</p>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<p style=\\\"text-align: center;\\\">&nbsp;</p> <p style=\\\"text-align: center;\\\">-ing</p>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Example:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">It is necessary to <span class=\"strong\">put off paying </span> licensing fees if the IT solution doesn't meet the company's needs. </span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "The following is a list of common verbs that are followed by the  infinite form of the verb:"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":1,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<p style=\\\"text-align: center;\\\">&nbsp;Decide<br />Need<br />Choose<br />Determine<br />Want</p>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<p style=\\\"text-align: center;\\\">&nbsp;</p> <p style=\\\"text-align: center;\\\">to verb</p>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Example:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">A company <span class=\"strong\">needs to assess </span> their IT needs. </span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Well, in IT systems negotiations there's something called acceptance tests, which involve putting new systems to test. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Depending on the results of these tests, the organization will determine to accept and pay for the installed system."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Benefits for successful implementation of an information technology system."}, {"type": "describer", "content": "In spite of the common risks and limitations when implementing an information technology solution, there are extraordinary benefits for any operation or project such as: "}, {"type": "text", "content": "<ul> <li>Easier access to organizational data</li> <li>Management of access security levels</li> <li>Error reduction</li> <li>Faster response time</li> <li>Cost savings</li> <li>Greater security</li> <li>Improved productivity</li> </ul>"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "internship"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a period of time in which a person gets practical experience in a profession or occupation "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: May I ask you some questions about the internship you did at the IT department in TRG Accounting?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n7le01ob07aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "do the job "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to achieve the expected result "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I guess every organization needs to choose whether they want to have their own customized software, or if a license would do the job."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n7le01ob07aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "ownership"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "legal statement of possession  "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: But what's most important are the ownership rights."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n7le01ob07aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "put off "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to delay or postpone "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(phrasal verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: This means that they can put off paying the vendors until the organization is sure that the procured products meet requirements and expectations."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n7le01ob07aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "not quite "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "not exactly"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Charles: I mean, when buying IT products, is the contract price paid up front? Sarah: Not quite."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n7le01ob07aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "agreement "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the arrangement between both parties related to a course of action"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: That means that the organization would only have licensed rights, unless it is specified otherwise in the contract agreement."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n7le01ob07aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Investigate how companies acquire IT services and how often they do it. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write a list of aspects companies have into account before getting IT services. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Share with a partner which are the most important advantages and disadvantages they found."}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I search information about IT services acquisition in my community."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I make a list using vocabulary and structures on IT services. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I discuss with a partner about the differences in our lists."}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"_data": [], "id": 0, "contents": [{}], "type": "welcome", "template_override": 1}, {"template_override": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"audiosrc": "enpe8n7le01ob07re2aud01", "images": [{"time": "100", "image": "enpe8n7le01ob07re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "<p><strong>Charles</strong>: Hey, Sarah. May I ask you some questions about the internship you did at the IT department in TRG Accounting?</p>\n<p><strong>Sarah</strong>: Sure! Go ahead.</p>\n<p><strong>Charles</strong>: What determines whether an organization needs to buy or license an IT solution?</p>\n<p><strong>Sarah</strong>: Well, that&rsquo;s a question they asked themselves when I was at TRG. I guess every organization needs to choose whether they want to have their own customized software, or if a license would do the job. So, it is necessary for an organization to assess which IT product best fits their needs. But what it&rsquo;s most important is the ownership rights.</p>\n<p><strong>Charles</strong>: How&rsquo;s that?</p>"}, {"time": "34300", "image": "enpe8n7le01ob07re2img02.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "<p><strong>Sarah</strong>: I mean, even if they buy their own IT solution, the developer would own the software. That means that the organization would only have licensed rights, unless it is specified otherwise in the contract agreement. That scenario might lead to additional fees, and no organization would ever want that.</p>\n<p><strong>Charles</strong>: I see your point. Now, what about the payments? I mean, when buying IT products, is the contract price paid up front?</p>\n<p><strong>Sarah</strong>: Not quite. It is true, though, that vendors often ask a big percentage of the contract price, but TRG would only pay under the acceptance of deliverables and services. This means that they can put off paying the vendors until the organization is sure that the procured products meet requirements and expectations.</p>"}, {"time": "77000", "image": "enpe8n7le01ob07re2img03.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "<p><strong>Charles</strong>: How do they make sure the products work just fine?</p>\n<p><strong>Sarah</strong>: Well, in IT systems negotiations there&rsquo;s something called acceptance tests, which involve putting new systems to test. These tests should be performed by the company or by an external consultant to ensure objectivity. Depending on the results of these tests, the organization will determine to accept and pay for the installed system.</p>"}], "coverimg": "enpe8n7le01ob07re2img01.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "type": "audio", "_data": [], "id": 1, "title": ""}], "exercises": [{"stimul